    "created_at": "2021-09-21T19:46:11Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-09-21T19:46:11Z",
    "body": "> This might be the culprit for PowerShell: https://github.com/starship/starship/blob/master/src/init/starship.ps1#L29\r\n\r\nCommenting this out/setting it to false is not really an option because then the prompt wouldn't appear at all.\r\n\r\nI guess we can implement an option to pass terminal width to the `starship prompt` command, with a flag like *--term-width*. PowerShell can use the `$Host.UI.RawUI.WindowSize.Width` variable and Bash can use `$COLUMNS` variable.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
